- op: discuss  # dd56
  at: '2026-09-09T03:31:18Z'  # dd56
  by: agent  # dd56
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dd56
  clock: 8  # dd56
  nonce: dd56  # dd56
  message: "DONE. Shipped in PR #843 (merged dev b207608f6f). The quadratic is REMOVED, not\nreduced, and the output is byte-identical.\n\nMEASURED AFTER, same curve, same repo, cold cache per run, sequential:\n\n    N       before     after   speedup   s/file before -> after   nodes b/a      edges b/a\n    150      63.3s     26.9s     2.36x   0.422 -> 0.179           3538/3538      12737/12737\n    300      74.7s     30.7s     2.43x   0.249 -> 0.102           4054/4054      13846/13846\n    600     287.0s     47.8s     6.01x   0.478 -> 0.080           9004/9004      34057/34057\n   1200    1700.0s     95.1s    17.88x   1.418 -> 0.079          21302/21302   113106/113106\n\n**NODES AND EDGES ARE IDENTICAL AT EVERY N**, and that check is the important\nhalf: a resolution change that got faster by resolving LESS would look like a win\nin a timing table and nowhere else.\n\nTHE SCALING PROPERTY, which is the actual claim rather than the headline: per-file\ncost over N=300 -> N=1200 was **5.70x** and is now **0.77x** -- flat, slightly\nDECREASING as fixed costs amortise. The speedup GROWS with N (2.36x -> 17.88x),\nwhich is the signature of removing a superlinear term rather than shaving a\nconstant. pretix now costs 0.079 s/file, BELOW kserve's pre-fix 0.198 -- kserve\nwas never the fast repository, it was the small one.\n\nWhole-survey wall on pretix: 1914.8s -> 342.95s.\n\nTHE FIX: the suffix and name indexes are cached on REGISTRY IDENTITY rather than\non the resolver, so `lookup_symbol`'s per-call fresh resolver reuses the built\nindex. Chosen over threading the existing optional `resolver` parameter through\nsix forwarding layers, because that parameter already existed, all nine py.go\ncall sites already passed it, and 46% of calls still arrived with None. An\noptional argument whose omission costs 6.7x is a footgun; the fast path is now\nthe default.\n\nTagged awaits_bakeoff_validation: 17.88x is a quantitative claim on one\nrepository, and the queue owns whether it reproduces elsewhere.\n\nWHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED, carried forward rather than closed over:\n  * Other languages. `NameResolver` / `ListNameResolver` have their own index\n    builders and were measured NEAR-FREE (0.0 s) in the profile, so they were\n    deliberately left alone -- fix what is measured. Whether another analyzer\n    hits the same shape is untested.\n  * Repositories other than pretix. kserve was not re-run; its python pass was\n    107 s and was never the subject.\n  * That no OTHER superlinear term remains. The curve says per-file cost is flat\n    from 300 to 1200 files. It says nothing above 1200.\n\nA COST MODEL THIS INVALIDATES, filed here so it is not discovered by surprise:\nmeasurement 0020's arms were priced at 35-46 minutes each BECAUSE of this\nquadratic. A reader planning a cohort from 0020's timings will now over-estimate\nby roughly 5x -- in the SAFE direction, but the pre-registration discipline says\na cost model gets corrected in writing rather than silently. 0020 is being\namended to say so."  # dd56
